            <div xml:id="d763">

                <pb facs="0947" n="857" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg857"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/126: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jefferson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-30T10:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">January 30,
                                1920—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3. Department’s January 24th 6 p.m. I have urged upon President Chamorro the
                    necessity of using all care in respecting his agreements regarding boundary
                    dispute and to apprehend if possible Honduraneans crossing border into
                    Nicaragua. He informed me that he is conscientiously living up to his
                    agreements.</p>
                <p>He informed me this morning he has just received telegram from his Chargé
                    d’Affaires in Honduras to the effect that Honduranean Government insists upon
                    his permitting it to send troops into Nicaragua to capture band of Honduranean
                    revolutionists. He telegraphed he would not agree to such an invasion of
                    Nicaraguan territory. He informed me he is sending a small guard to the border
                    to prevent raids and to watch movements of Honduranean troops.</p>
                <pb facs="0948" n="858" xml:id="pg858"/>
                <p>The President seems much concerned and urges upon the Department the necessity of
                    bringing boundary dispute to an early and final settlement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
